state/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.lavish/
.venv/
# No trailing slash: the deploy worker links the live venv into its tree (keel/deploy.py).
.venv-voice

# A segment's generated output is never repo content. Every fetcher run rewrites data/
# and summary.json, so tracking either leaves the checkout dirty on a schedule. These
# rules land before any segment is copied in, so a fetch pass between the copy and the
# commit cannot stage one. instamart's inbox/ is the same thing under another name: the
# app drops uploaded invoice PDFs there and fetch.py reads them.
segments/*/data/
segments/*/summary.json
segments/instamart/inbox/

# The install's own config (c-610 S1): its user's choices and its machine's paths, never
# repo content. etc/shipyard.example.toml is what the installer copies there.
/config.toml

# Services are rendered per machine (`keel/service.py`) with that machine's paths, into an
# install's services/, or a bare checkout's etc/: never repo content.
etc/*.service
etc/*.timer
etc/*.plist

# One owner's own things, which live in that owner's install since c-722: a config an older
# checkout kept, and the memory and profile it kept before the move.
/keel.toml
/talker/memory/
/identity/

# The personal space's config dir on a machine where it lives inside the checkout (the box
# had one before c-622). Never repo content: it holds skills that are not Keel's and, on
# Linux, the login.
spaces/personal/

# The staging boards the cutover sets aside beside state/ on the box. Runtime data, like
# state/ itself: never tracked, and never read by the drift guard in `make test`.
state.staging-*/
